.venv/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.gif
node_modules/
tests/
scripts/
data/
# ...except the highlight pool, which the bot reads at runtime. Excluding
# the directory and then COPYing a file out of it does not fail loudly at
# runtime — it fails the build, which on Render means the old container
# keeps serving and the deploy is "done" as far as anyone watching the URL
# can tell. tests/test_docker_build_context.py checks the two files agree.
!data/highlights.json
!data/term_index.json
# The clipper's source of the media URL and the per-second segments.
# Gzipped because the raw file is 7.6MB and every ingest rewrites it.
!data/episodes.json.gz
!data/elon_episodes.json.gz
!data/mcg_index.json
!data/mcg_summaries.json.gz
# Which broadcast player each X episode's citations should point at. Read
# when a deep link is BUILT, so without it in the image every broadcast
# citation silently falls back to the status url — which is the link that
# X renders as an unclickable card. The deploy looks fine; the timestamps
# just stop working.
!data/broadcast_links.json
# Read at runtime too, and each one failed safe and silently without it:
# the YouTube map (every citation stayed on X), the guest windows (the bot
# answered "who was on" with "not read yet" for every episode), and the
# speaker map (clips lost their names). tests/test_docker_build_context.py
# now checks every data file the app opens is here.
!data/youtube_map.json
!data/guest_windows.json
!data/speaker_map.json
redteam_report.md
PITCH_PREP.md
